{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881343-where-does-sculpture-belong-as-a-skill","id":881343,"title":"Where does Sculpture belong as a skill?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-03T16:21:39-07:00","id":881343,"title":"Where does Sculpture belong as a skill?","content":"Crafts has Sculpting as a Specialty, but the skill doesn't really seem to mention the application.<br /> Expression doesn't, but then specialties aren't meant to be exhaustive, but it it pretty explicitly the &quot;art&quot; skill.<br /> <br /> Is this a difference in application? Like - they're both the skills for Sculpture, but Crafts is &quot;practical&quot; sculpting, whatever that may be? Or maybe it counts for decoration in terms of large building projects? Or does Sculpting here refer to something else?<br /> Do Pottery and making clothing count under Crafts or Expression?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm blind.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">It covers writing and spoken communication, art like painting or sculpture</span></span> </div> </div> </div>~ Still, what does Sculpting in Crafts refer to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 05-03-2016, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T16:33:48-07:00","id":881352,"title":"","content":"If nothing else, there are non-artistic applications of sculpting. While CAD and 3D printing is taking over a lot of this space, sculpting scale models to mock up possible product designs, as well as doing things like sculpting forensic recreations of the features of skeletons, and so on.<br /> <br /> I could also see it applied to sculpting things like molds for the production of various items.<br /> <br /> Basically, while it is a fuzzy line, I'd draw it between sculpting solely to create a work of art that evokes emotion, and sculpting for a practical application.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T17:05:18-07:00","id":881365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/881343-where-does-sculpture-belong-as-a-skill#post881343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crafts has Sculpting as a Specialty, but the skill doesn't really seem to mention the application.<br /> Expression doesn't, but then specialties aren't meant to be exhaustive, but it it pretty explicitly the &amp;quot;art&amp;quot; skill.<br /> <br /> Is this a difference in application? Like - they're both the skills for Sculpture, but Crafts is &amp;quot;practical&amp;quot; sculpting, whatever that may be? Or maybe it counts for decoration in terms of large building projects? Or does Sculpting here refer to something else?<br /> Do Pottery and making clothing count under Crafts or Expression?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm blind.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ Still, what does Sculpting in Crafts refer to?</div> </div> </div> </div>The following paragraph answers your question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is some overlap between this Skill and the Crafts Skill. Expression is generally used when trying to create a piece of artwork specifically for aesthetic or emotional reasons, as opposed to making an accurate copy or model, which uses Crafts. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}